<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abgar V</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 50 CE</span> · Also known as Abgar V of Edessa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abgar V was a king of Osroene who ruled from Edessa in the early 1st century CE. Christian tradition, recorded by Eusebius, claims that he exchanged letters with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a> and was healed by the disciple Addai, and the later legend of the Image of Edessa grew from this story. The tradition made Edessa an early centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syriac">Syriac</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abgar-v.jpg" alt="Abgar V" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous (Category:Artists)Unknown author. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abgarwithimageofedessa10thcentury.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
